WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.260
<i>Two more. No...</i>

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.280
<i>I'm pumped.</i>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.830
Jota!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.610
Jota!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.580
<i>Hana?</i>

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.000
<i>What's she doing here?</i>

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.180
<i>Wasn't she watching
the starting line at Otemachi?</i>

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.460
You can do it!

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.590
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.550
<i>No, but—</i>

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.020
<i>Does she like me?</i>

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:48.020
<i>What? Seriously?!</i>

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:01.990
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.490
Bro!

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.340
Oh, wow!

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.530
He's so strong during the actual event.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.880
Joji!

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:40.840
Hey!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.300
Hana!

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.260
Huh?

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.720
I think...

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:50.850
...she likes me.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.240
Seriously?!

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.740
What? But Hana—

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.370
Seriously?!

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.200
Come here, you idiot!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.790
<b><i>Even If I Break</i></b>

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:16.460
<b>Section 4</b>

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:12.800
<i>Kansei is still catching up.</i>

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:13.860
<i>Since finishing last in Section 1,</i>

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.070
<i>their position has steadily climbed
to their current 10th place.</i>

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.160
<i>At this rate, they might even
catch Tokyo Sport in 9th.</i>

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.470
<i>I see.</i>

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.880
<i>Seriously? I see.</i>

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:29.850
Did Hana herself say that she likes Jota?

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.850
No, it's not like that.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:35.810
I simply thought she liked one of the twins.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.150
Well, he's suddenly assuming she does.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.530
He even told Joji.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.620
Why would that idiot agitate
his brother like that?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.670
<i>Hana's on her way to Odawara.</i>

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:49.950
Who is she? Godzilla?

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:55.380
Should we have the coach tell
him Jota's confused about Hana?

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.890
I've never heard of that kind
of instruction being given before.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.450
I'll make the decision.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.090
Not that I'm happy with it.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.800
<b>Section 4</b>

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.010
Run, you idiot!

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:12.610
<i>It doesn't make sense
that she likes him, though.</i>

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:16.190
<i>She was always with the two of us.</i>

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.440
<i>When did she develop feelings for him?</i>

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.690
<i>Maybe he meant as a friend.</i>

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:23.790
<i>In that case...</i>

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:28.630
<i>No, in that case, I like Hana as a friend, too.</i>

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.850
<i>Just as a friend.</i>

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.880
<i>Yeah, a friend...</i>

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.120
Want some help?

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.560
Thanks. Joji, could you take out that garbage?

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.840
Okay.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.430
Hey, Hana...

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.140
How can you tell us apart?

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.390
What?

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:57.780
You didn't have think when you used my name.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.570
Oh. No one at Aotake gets you mixed up.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.360
Well, yeah.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.940
I've never thought about
trying to tell you apart.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:11.040
Since the day I met you,
you were you, and Jota was Jota.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:15.450
You're brothers and best
friends and always together,

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.750
but what I like about each of you is...

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.400
Never mind.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.210
Hey!

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.340
We're gonna start lighting fireworks!

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.560
No way! I'm coming!

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.720
Hey, Joji!

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.350
Are you listening? Answer me!

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:39.890
<i>He's really mad.</i>

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:42.320
<i>How much did I miss?</i>

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.250
Jeez.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:48.440
I'm not sure what it means, but you
have a message from Kurahara.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:49.700
Just listen.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.440
<i>From Kakeru?</i>

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.960
“If you like her, run.”

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.270
That's all.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:03.640
It's what I was told to say.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.650
<i>Who does he think he is?</i>

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.130
<i>But...</i>

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.560
<b>Odahara Relay Station</b>

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.020
He handed me the phone. It's me.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.980
Sounds pretty noisy over there.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.980
Yes. We're all anxious to start.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:28.700
Shindo.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.330
What'd he say?

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:39.730
That I'd better hydrate.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:42.580
It's the same for everyone.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.710
There's nothing left to say.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.890
Congratulations Takashi on
Running in the Hakone Ekiden

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:58.810
<b>Certain Victory</b>

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:01.440
They're almost at Section 5!

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.810
He's gonna run!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.070
It might not be colder than over there. Is everyone there?

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.070
Yeah, everyone's already in front of the TV. Our uncle from Tsuruoka just arrived!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.070
Kansei University is amazing! Yu said he's rooting for you. I'm starting to feel nervous.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.070
I'll do my best.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.070
First place, brother!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.030
First place, brother!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:25.460
<b>Section 4</b>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.350
Rikudo was too slow.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:23.090
The champions are slowly falling behind.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:27.130
Currently in first place is Boso's Saito.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.450
Rikudo is also within range of Daiwa in third.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.990
Saikyo is coming! Saikyo!

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:58.950
I'd better go.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.810
Tokyo Sport is next!

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:02.800
Tokyo Sport to the relay line!

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.250
But it's Section 5.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.790
Actually, no matter the section—

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.580
Kansei, Kikui! Get ready!

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.950
They're coming at the same time!

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:13.890
It's okay.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.730
I promise I'll make it there.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:34.220
<i>No matter what.</i>

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.420
Damn it!

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:51.900
Joji?

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:56.300
Damn it. What did I do?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:00.560
Why couldn't I go faster?

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.310
He was hot.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.230
Hotter than me, and I'd just run Section 4.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.880
I knew.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:21.610
I knew I had to get us
as much time as possible,

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:23.870
but I...

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:25.730
Raise your head.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:27.580
He's already running.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.300
<i>This is Car 3.</i>

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:34.510
<i>Kansei's Sugiyama's pace
is remaining constant.</i>

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:38.800
<i>Kikui's Inagaki is already 500 meters ahead.</i>

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.380
<i>Kansei has suddenly hit the brakes.</i>

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.560
Brother?

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:49.750
<i>Yokohama and Jonan Bunka
are catching up from behind.</i>

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.000
<i>Will he be able to stay ahead of them?</i>

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:53.030
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.750
<i>No, it's just a matter of time.</i>

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.950
<b>Section 5</b>

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.910
<i>He seems to be having some kind of problem.</i>

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.130
Kansei, you can do it!

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.340
<i>It wouldn't surprise us if he stopped anytime.</i>

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:52.220
You can do it!

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:55.200
<i>Will he be able to make it over
the mountains of Hakone?</i>

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:06.380
<i>Shindo, go is a challenging game.</i>

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.940
<i>The stronger you are, the more
you value the way you lose.</i>

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:17.850
How you recognize your loss and resign is key.

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:23.450
<i>No one blames the challenger for
resigning or mocks him for running away.</i>

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:28.380
If anything, they praise him
for securing an escape route.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.380
<i>It's because everyone knows
that man was fighting to win</i>

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.950
<i>until the very end.</i>

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>Shindo, raise your hand if you can't keep going.</i>

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:54.380
I'll stop you immediately.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:09.660
<i>The lead runners are approaching
the finish line at Lake Ashi.</i>

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.430
<i>Their first first-half victory in four
years is right before their eyes.</i>

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.830
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:17.760
<i>A new god has descended upon Hakone!</i>

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:23.450
<i>Boso second-year Yanase Wataru
finishes in a new section record!</i>

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:26.070
<i>Boso wins the first half!</i>

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:29.890
<i>I'm here with Kansei.</i>

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:33.570
<i>Kansei's Coach Tazaki
has gotten out of the car.</i>

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:36.940
<i>Will he stop Sugiyama and forfeit the race?</i>

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:43.110
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:46.820
<i>He's stopped! Sugiyama has finally stopped!</i>

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.750
That's enough. You did well.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.530
No!

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:29.770
Hey.

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.180
Waiting...

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:37.670
They're all waiting for me...

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:48.760
<i>Why are we so desperate to keep running?</i>

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:55.660
<i>Why can't we stop doing something
so painful and difficult?</i>

00:13:56.530 --> 00:14:00.060
<i>For our friends. For our goals. For ourselves.</i>

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.050
<i>Stubbornness and pride.</i>

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.800
<i>I don't know. I doubt anyone knows.</i>

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:10.350
<i>That's why we can't look away.</i>

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.640
<i>That's why it sticks in our hearts.</i>

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.520
Shindo!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:04.590
<b>Ashihara Inn</b>

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:10.950
<i>Kansei's Sugiyama Takashi is
experiencing difficulties in Section 5.</i>

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.550
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:27.030
<b>Hakone – Lake Ashi</b>

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:14.710
<i>While periodically stopping, he brushes
off his coach's attempts to stop him</i>

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:18.280
<i>and finishes all 20.7 kilometers of Section 5.</i>

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:21.840
<i>Sugiyama is greeted by 
a continuous wave of cheers</i>

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:27.030
<b>First Half 20th – Kansei University</b>

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:24.730
<i>after demonstrating that he has
the strongest will in the country.</i>

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:29.380
We've already called your family.

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:33.980
They said they'd come take care of you,
but we politely declined their offer.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:43.550
Shindo finished his section,
but tomorrow will be a difficult battle.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:44.750
It won't be!

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:49.670
Because you'll run?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:55.580
I'm glad you're confident, but sometimes
making it to the end isn't good enough.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:01.510
Tomorrow, I won't let you boys expose
yourselves to the same kind of danger.

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:04.810
We'll be fully prepared for tomorrow.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:08.780
Switching our focus to that comes first.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:11.490
Yes, sir.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:14.060
I'm sorry.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:20.840
Once you've prepared
for tomorrow, call the others.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:22.040
You haven't yet, right?

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.760
They must be anxious.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:34.250
Go ahead.

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:37.970
<i>Nice work.</i>

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:38.690
<i>Shindo!</i>

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.810
<i>Musa, there's no point in getting any closer!</i>

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.640
<i>You'll be fine as long as
you're not dead, Shindo!</i>

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.360
Guys.

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:56.030
You worked hard today.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:58.240
We'll have more chances tomorrow!

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:02.240
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:03.830
<i>Who was that?</i>

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.220
<i>Probably King.</i>

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:06.750
<i>What does that mean?</i>

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.880
Shut up. Be quiet.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:12.910
If you're running tomorrow, stay warm
while you sleep and don't overeat.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:13.900
That's all.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:14.970
That's all?!

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.640
<i>Don't you have any more helpful advice?</i>

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.260
No.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.350
<i>Hey!</i>

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:22.300
It'll be over after tomorrow.

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:25.100
All we can do is focus, so we
can give everything we've got.

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:34.360
Excuse me. Why don't we do that?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.320
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:42.020
I'm sure yours will feel the most authentic.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.040
Let's do it.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:52.380
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:54.620
The steepest in the world!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:06.390
It might snow tomorrow.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.280
Kakeru.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.840
Was that your parents' idea?

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.280
You mean my name? Yes.

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:15.190
My father ran track.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:18.300
Did your father push you towards running, too?

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:21.160
No. Our communication was never...

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.490
Wait! Why do you ask?

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:32.790
My father is a high school track coach.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:35.050
I was one of his runners.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:42.210
He's not a bad person.
He just loves track to a fault.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:45.810
I didn't have time to think
while under his total supervision,

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.160
and I ran every day.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:50.980
Eventually, I broke.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:29.730
But...

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:35.190
Unable to run for the first time,
I genuinely wanted to run.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:51.120
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:53.670
This time, I'll share a dream with
teammates who earnestly want to run.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.290
Whether they're weak or amateurs,

00:19:56.720 --> 00:20:01.550
as long as they've got talent and
passion, I'm sure they can run.

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:11.340
For that, I bent everyone to my will.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:18.690
We knew there was only ten of us.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.250
But we're more than ten.

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:24.270
The shopping center vendors, the university,
and the people far away from us

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:26.820
are all part of the team.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:29.180
No one thinks you forced them to do anything.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:34.460
Even if you did, don't forget
that I'm grateful for that.

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:36.840
Let's run.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:43.150
We're going to run the best we ever have.

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:45.900
<b>Next time: Goodbye, Beautiful World</b>

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:44.360
Next time, “Goodbye, Beautiful World.”
